ath  machi is the third member of the group  and she's probably one of the least  expressive or personable among the group  however it has been shown that she  actually does care about the group  despite this  honestly i've always had a soft spot for  mochi specifically because of her nen  abilities and you know she's also super  cute but either way machi can create  strings out of nen and if you know how  much i love vanessa in black clover you  know i'm pretty much down for this we've  seen her use this in two different ways  firstly she can create nen stitches  which can help to reattach limbs and  help with several minor injuries as well  or she can use nen threads to bind or  choke her opponents or just take control  of their movements like puppets while  these threads are still attached to  machi they are nearly invincible meaning  you can neither cut or rip them but once  she lets go this durability stops  our first look at number four was hisoka  he is entirely chaotic and willing to do  or work with anyone necessary to get a  fight with someone powerful at the end  of the day he is team hisoka and if that  means pretending to be a troop member  for a short period of time because he  wants to fight crollo then he's probably  going to do that the downside of this  being that he's a little too interested  in power and potential and even if  someone is i don't know for example a  young boy with spiky hair he becomes  completely devoted to the idea of  fighting them even to the point of  arousal but yeah at the end of the day  he's just a sociopathic clown who  falsely joined the troop to get his  rocks off at the chance of fighting the  leader hisoka is likely one of the most  well-rounded people in the entire series  in terms of power let alone just in the  troop this isn't to say he's unstoppable  by any means but he is fast strong  sneaky and smart enough to keep up with  just about anyone he can come across on  top of that he's durable enough to keep  the battle going if the person  overpowers him he also has a pretty big  leg up in most battles due to his nen  ability bungie gum which has the  property of both rubber and gum bungee  gum is basically an aura that hisoka can  exude from his body to create elastic  threads barriers or glue as well as a  slew of other things he can attach this  to any kind of surface that he wants to  gain an advantage through manipulating  his environment he really is only  limited by his ingenuity in a way that  most other nen users aren't and his  ability to think on his feet and use his  bungee gum in new and dynamic ways makes  him one of the most interesting  characters in the series when it comes  to fights he can also attach or detach  bungie gum to people or objects as well  creating slings or even drawing his  opponents in for free hits  if projectiles are coming for him he can  just make a wall of bungee gum to launch  them back or he can even just apply it  to the soles of his feet to keep his  position steady this ability honestly  feels like he could do just about  anything if hisoka has enough time to  figure out the situation we also saw him  use bungie gum in a more manipulative  and tricky way in texture surprise  basically he uses his aura and bungee  gum to apply materials to his skin and  replicate a desired look and feel we saw  him using this to confuse castro to hide  his wounds and we also saw him using  this to apply a fake phantom troop  tattoo on himself to show false loyalty  however he left the group pretty early  on and was replaced by kaluto zoldik  kaluto is both the youngest and weakest  member of the troop and while he was  with the zoldix he was essentially just  a very quiet and obedient person that  said once he joins the troop he begins  opening up quite a bit  kaluto is just kind of a super cool  character altogether just like kilauea  he has been trained to be an assassin so  he's very stealthy and can use rhythm  echo and also just like kilauea he has a  pretty unique weapon using a paper fan  that said he can empower this fan to  even be strong enough to cut steel  speaking of paper though most of  kaluto's nen abilities revolve around it  he can make paper dolls of a person that  he attached a piece of confetti to and  after doing so he'll be able to hear  anything that happens around that person  super useful for gathering information  then there's the dance of the serpent  fang which is where he drops a bunch of  confetti and then forms it into a giant  snake-like cyclone of paper that tears  enemies apart and he can do this on  repeat if needed number five is finx who  to me at least probably has my least  favorite male character design in the  group mostly because like  well look at him he's just kind of a  dude anyways as you might guess by  looking at him he's pretty quick to  anger and get into arguments with the  other members but overall he still does  get along with them while we do have  some information on his nen we still  really don't know the limits of what he  can do yet he is a great hand-to-hand  fighter in just about every sense but  when he needs to he can also use  ripper's cyclotron this is the only net  ability we've seen from him so far and  it sees him spinning his arm in a  clockwise fashion with each revolution  storing power for his next attack for  reference it took about 15 spins to kill  a chimera ant but he did say that half  that much would have been fine next up  we have a bit of a confusing situation  as number six and nine is either shall  narc or pakunoda each of these members  is unfortunately dead now so we can't  exactly ask them to figure it out and  these are also the first positions which  we haven't seen replaced yet after the  character is passed on let's start with  pakunoda because it kind of follows the  trend of being a dull character design  that said as a character she's pretty  great beyond that  very proud and intimidating but also  super loyal to the p